          kind: "concept",
          refs: ['g5.24.16', 'g5.24.25'],
          lemma: "μεταβέβηκεν ἐκ τοῦ θανάτου εἰς τὴν ζωήν",
          title: "Already passed from death to life",
          body: "The tenses are the miracle: the believer **has** (present) eternal life and **has passed** (perfect — a completed move with lasting result) out of death into life. The great verdict is not only future; it is pronounced *now*, the moment one hears Jesus’ word and trusts the Father who sent him. This is John’s hallmark — “eternal life” as a present possession, and the resurrection begun already in those who believe (v. 25). Death is behind them, not merely ahead.",
