          kind: "concept",
          refs: ['g5.44.5', 'g5.44.11'],
          lemma: "δόξαν παρὰ ἀλλήλων",
          title: "Why they cannot believe",
          body: "Jesus names the deep root of unbelief, and it is not intellectual: they trade **glory (honor) with one another** — living for each other’s approval — and so cannot **seek the glory that comes from the one God**. A heart bent on human esteem is structurally unable to receive a Messiah who comes lowly and hands all glory to the Father. Faith, on this diagnosis, is finally a matter of *whose approval you are living for*.",
