          lemma: "περὶ ἐμοῦ ἐκεῖνος ἔγραψεν",
          title: "“Moses wrote about me”",
          body: "The great irony lands: the people staking everything on Moses will find **Moses their accuser**, because Moses *wrote about Jesus* — the promised prophet like himself (Deut 18:15), the whole law and its sacrifices leaning forward. To reject Christ is not to defend Moses but to disbelieve him. And the closing sting (v. 47): if they will not believe Moses’ *writings*, how will they believe Jesus’ *words*? The Scriptures they trust and the Christ before them stand or fall together.",
